{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792943479,"nonce":"Rwg/nd1hWBXPE2nGsO/VvVmpsGg=","title":"RayDE in the browser: editor UI in a page, workspaces and extension processes mounted from a cloud session","message":"**Goal**\n\nThe editor UI runs in a browser page. The workspace (files, git, language server, extension processes) lives on a remote session, preferably one Cloudflare Durable Object per session, and the page mounts it. First consumer: a code playground on the Rayzor landing page. Some features stay native-only.\n\n**What already exists (verified 2026-10-25)**\n\n- ashui runs in a page through Ash's wasm32-wasip1-threads target (ashui git-bug 0c8c9a0, docs/web.md): blinc_abi.wasm, xgpu.wasm (WebGPU) and xwindow.wasm are side modules beside the program. No filesystem in the page; assets are embedded with `ashui.core.Assets.embed`.\n- libgit2 1.9.7 builds for wasm with emscripten and works: init, index add, commit, revwalk and tree-to-workdir diff pass under Node. 800 KB wasm (286 KB gzipped). Needs `-DUSE_SSH=OFF -DUSE_HTTPS=OFF -DUSE_THREADS=OFF -DUSE_SHA1=CollisionDetection -DUSE_SHA256=Builtin -DREGEX_BACKEND=builtin`, `-Wno-incompatible-pointer-types` (size_t is unsigned long but SIZE_MAX == UINT_MAX on wasm32, so the add/multiply overflow intrinsics get the wrong pointer type) and a link stack of at least 1 MiB (`-sSTACK_SIZE=1048576`; the 64 KiB default overflows in lock_file). Clone, fetch and push need a custom transport over fetch(); local operations work as they are.\n- rayzor `parser`, `diagnostics` and `source_map` compile for wasm32-unknown-unknown unchanged.\n\n**What blocks the Rayzor language server in a page**\n\n`cargo check --target wasm32-unknown-unknown -p compiler --no-default-features` fails on three dependencies, all pulled in unconditionally:\n- cranelift-jit (through `region`): JIT memory. Only the backends need it.\n- rayzor-runtime (rustls, aws-lc-sys): the MIR lowering references runtime symbols in about twenty files under compiler/src/ir. Those need to come from rayzor-runtime-core or a table, not the full runtime.\n- zstd-sys: blade cache compression in compiler/src/ir/blade.rs. ruzstd or lz4_flex would build for wasm.\nThe lsp crate itself uses std::fs and a few libc calls in context.rs, editor_cache.rs, project.rs, stdlib.rs, workspace_index.rs and transport.rs (stdio). In a page its filesystem is the session's, so it needs a file-provider seam.\n\n**Native pieces RayDE loads**\n\n- rayscript.hdll (markdown, TOML, images, extension VM, Jam): pure Rust, but also pulls portable-pty-free code only; needs a wasm build of rayscript-vm and a check of irosashi, latex-rust, mermaid-rs-renderer.\n- cterm.hdll (terminal): portable-pty and vt100. vt100 parsing works in a page; the pty cannot. The terminal must be a stream to the session.\n- Jam (yrs, tokio-tungstenite): yrs builds for wasm; the transport is the browser's WebSocket, not tokio.\n- libgit2 (git extension natives): wasm build above.\n- sys.io.Process (8 files) and sys.FileSystem/File (58 files): the session boundary.\n\n**Plan, in order**\n\n1. Session protocol and workspace provider: files, watch, search, process spawn and PTY, as one interface RayDE calls instead of sys.*. Native implements it locally; the page implements it over a WebSocket to the session.\n2. RayDE as a wasm program in ashui's web lane, with the session provider and no terminal, git or language server: open a workspace, edit, highlight, Problems from a remote build.\n3. Language server: gate rayzor compiler for a frontend-only wasm build, run it in the session first (Durable Object, or a Container where a process is needed) and in the page later.\n4. Git: libgit2 wasm as a side module on a virtual filesystem, with the transport over fetch.\n5. Extension host: rayscript-vm in a worker or in the session.\n6. Playground embed for the Rayzor landing page.\n\n**Open questions**\n\nA Durable Object runs JS and wasm only: no processes, so Rayzor's compiler and language server run there as wasm, and anything that needs a real process (haxe, caribou, a PTY) needs a Cloudflare Container behind the object.","files":null}]}